course: dictionary
lesson: 7849
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Radio is a good example. Read the words around it before you decide.
explain: «It sends the numbers by invisible radio waves to the nearest phone mast» is about waves that carry signals, not a box you listen to. Ask: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «"A face for radio" is a joking, unkind way to say someone is ugly.» The sentence explains the phrase for you. Phrases like this are fixed, so you learn them as a group of words, not one word at a time.
explain: Radio can also be a verb. To radio someone is to send them a message by radio, so «radioed» means sent a message by radio. When you meet a new form of a word, check whether it is a noun or a verb in the sentence.
fact: A radio is a machine that receives sounds sent through the air by electric waves.
fact: The radio is the programmes sent out this way, such as music, news and talk.
fact: Radio waves are invisible waves that travel at the speed of light.
fact: Pilots, police and ships use radio to send messages, and a walkie-talkie is a small two-way radio.
fact: Guglielmo Marconi sent radio signals across the Atlantic in 1901.
exercise: «The radio was playing music in the kitchen.» What is a radio here? | A flat piece of wood for cooking | A message written on paper | *A machine that receives sounds sent through the air | A kind of bird that sings
exercise: «"A face for radio" is a joking way to say someone is what?» | *Ugly, in an unkind way | Very tall | Famous on television | Kind and clever
exercise: Pilots and ships use radio to do what? | Cook their food | Grow plants in the sea | *Send messages
test: «In the storm, the family listened to the wind-up radio for warnings.» What did the radio give them? | Heat for the room | *News and warnings | Clean water | Shelter from the rain
test: «The captain radioed the coast guard for help.» What does radioed mean? | Rang a bell | Wrote a letter by hand | *Sent a message by radio | Sailed away very fast
exam: In «Walkie-talkies are small two-way radios», what is a radio? | A type of meal | *A machine that sends and receives messages | A bus that travels between towns | A kind of musical instrument
